    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (69.61) and **Cal Raleigh** (69.52) headline the LawDog lineup as our strongest plays. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 13% dynamic platoon boost against Ure\u00f1a, positioning him to capitalize on a favorable matchup without the tax of facing an elite arm. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** remains a focal point; his placement in the #3 hole combined with a beneficial platoon split against Cantillo allows his raw power metrics to shine despite the 4.20 xERA hurdle. **Jonathan Aranda** also warrants attention, as his 67.60 score is bolstered by a significant 12% platoon edge and a strong #2 spot in the order, making him an elite play despite a slight park penalty in GABP.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest call today was keeping **Gavin Sheets** (57.47) in the starting nine over potential utility alternatives. **Gavin Sheets** occupies the threshold of our \"Marginal\" bucket, but his sustained 14% SP skill advantage against Sasaki kept him ahead of the pack. The primary reason we aren't seeing more upside from the rest of the bottom-order is the presence of high-hold-rate pitchers limiting stolen base opportunities for speed threats like **Masyn Winn** and **Daulton Varsho**. While **Masyn Winn** carries a sub-50 score, he remains in the lineup due to the scarcity of speed, though owners should monitor if the 3.68 xERA of Meyer effectively neutralizes his base-stealing lanes today.\n\nWe are operating with limited depth given the IL status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, which keeps our bench largely static. **Tyler Freeman** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but with official lineups confirming he is on the bench, he remains an inefficient start relative to our current projection model. We must keep a close watch on **Jung Hoo Lee**, as his 63.61 score is heavily predicated on an favorable platoon split against L\u00f3pez; should the weather or late-inning defensive substitutions shift, his impact in the outfield could be dampened. Otherwise, we are leaning heavily into the platoon advantages held by **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** to stabilize our AVG and RBI counts against a soft matchup.",
